  "title": "ProductQueuePage uses /api/v1/admin/ endpoint prefix instead of /api/v1/retailer-admin/admin/",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: API Integration. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. ProductQueuePage makes API calls to `/api/v1/admin/products/pending` (line 85), `/api/v1/admin/products/{id}/edit` (line 167), `/api/v1/admin/products/{id}/approve` (line 183), and `/api/v1/admin/products/{id}/reject` (line 240). These use the `/api/v1/admin/` prefix, which routes to the superadmin gateway, not the retailer-admin gateway. This means: (1) Auth cookies may not be sent to the correct service, (2) The API gateway may not apply retailer-specific middleware (store isolation, RBAC), (3) The endpoints may 404 if the superadmin service doesn't mount these routes.",
